# ASP.NET Core Staff Administration Portal Design

## Phase 2 – System Architecture and Design

### Developer
Kamohelo Mohlohlo  
Role: Web Developer – ASP.NET Core

## Purpose

The ASP.NET Core web portal will provide Mangojane Funeral Parlour staff
with an administrative interface for managing funeral operations.

The portal will connect to the same Supabase backend used by the Flutter
Client application. This will allow information created from the mobile
application to become available to authorised staff.

## Planned Staff Portal Functions

The ASP.NET Core portal will allow authorised staff to:

- Log into the staff administration portal.
- View an operational dashboard.
- View and manage Client funeral bookings.
- Review individual booking information.
- Approve or reject funeral bookings.
- Assign available resources to approved bookings.
- Allocate hearses, drivers and equipment.
- View the daily dispatch schedule.
- Search burial society policy information.
- Record premium payments.
- View operational reports.
- Manage authorised system users.
- Manage staff profile information.
- Log out securely.

## Booking Management Flow

The planned booking workflow will be:

Client Mobile Application
→ Supabase
→ ASP.NET Core Staff Portal
→ Staff Reviews Booking
→ Approve or Reject Booking
→ Allocate Resources
→ Update Supabase
→ Updated Status Available to Client

When a Client submits a funeral booking through the Flutter application,
the booking will be stored in Supabase.

Supabase Realtime will be used so that new or updated booking information
can become available to the ASP.NET Core portal without staff having to
manually refresh the system.

The system has a target synchronization time of less than three seconds.
This is currently a system requirement and will need to be verified during
implementation and testing.

## Resource Allocation

For approved bookings, staff will be able to allocate operational
resources such as:

- Hearse
- Driver
- Funeral tent
- Chairs
- Family vehicles
- Other required funeral equipment

The system will check resource availability before an allocation is
confirmed to reduce scheduling conflicts.

## Burial Society and Premium Management

The staff portal will provide functionality for searching burial society
policies and recording premium payments.

The current prototype will record payment information manually.
Integration with a live payment gateway is outside the current project
scope.

## Daily Dispatch and Reporting

The portal will provide a Daily Dispatch Schedule showing funeral
assignments and allocated resources.

Staff will also have access to reporting functionality for daily
operational information.

